# One 429 rate-limit error then success: humaniseRetryError
# (internal/tui/bridge.go ~1023) renders "429 rate limited" wording for a
# 429 status.
@faux testdata/faux/qa/errors-429-rate-limited.yaml

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
SHOT welcome
TYPE ask while rate limited
SHOT typed
KEY enter
# EXPECT runs a fresh screen read at the moment it executes, not the
# SHOT's capture, so the 1s countdown could tick past (or the retry could
# finish) between SHOT and EXPECT; check the transient text immediately
# after WAITFOR observes it, then SHOT for evidence.
WAITFOR /Stream interrupted · 429 rate limited/ 20
EXPECT /Retrying in \ds · attempt 2 of 4 · r to retry now/
SHOT countdown
WAITFOR /Reconnected on attempt 2/ 10
SHOT reconnected
WAITFOR /Back within the rate limit/ 10
SHOT reply
EXPECT /Back within the rate limit/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
